course: dictionary
lesson: 10884
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so read the words around them to find the one that fits. «The shop sold vintage clothes from the 1960s.» Here vintage means old but of good quality, from an earlier time.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. A wine label may show a vintage, which is the year its grapes were picked. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence and whether the rest of the text agrees.
explain: In Melbourne a girl says, «Isn't that your sister's dress?» Coco twirls: «Yeah, it's vintage, babe.» Everyone laughs, with her. Here vintage is informal for old and used, and the laughing shows it is said in a friendly, joking way.
fact: Vintage means old but of good quality, from an earlier time: vintage clothes, a vintage car.
fact: The vintage of a wine is the year or season when its grapes were picked.
fact: In informal talk, vintage can mean typical of someone at their best: «that joke was vintage Grandpa».
fact: Vintage shops sell old clothes, toys and furniture, and vintage car shows display old cars.
fact: Useful phrases: a good vintage, vintage style, vintage clothes.
exercise: «The shop sold vintage clothes from the 1960s.» What does vintage mean here? | Made of plastic | *Old but good quality, from an earlier time | Very cheap and broken | Brand new from the shop
exercise: A wine label says «2015 vintage». What does vintage mean on this label? | The colour of the bottle | The shop where it was sold | The price of the wine | *The year the grapes were picked
exercise: «That joke was vintage Grandpa.» What does vintage suggest here? | *Typical of him at his best | He bought it at a shop | He told it in 1950 | He forgot the joke
test: Coco says «Yeah, it's vintage, babe.» Everyone laughs with her. What does this tell you? | They are sad about the dress | They are angry with her | *They are joking along with her in a friendly way | They want to buy the dress
test: Which of these is a vintage car? | *A car made many years ago that is still valued and well kept | A car made in a factory with no name | A toy car from a shop | A car made last week
exam: Which meaning of vintage fits «a good vintage» on a bottle of wine? | *The year the grapes were picked | A type of shop | A cheap price | A old, used bottle
